{'id': 78, 'parent_id': 75, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'riverwell', 'title': '', 'body': 'I’ve had this when a plugin changed the default timezone. Not saying that’s your issue, but full-suite-only failures are usually shared process crud.', 'created': 1789092874.6096566}
{'id': 80, 'parent_id': 79, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'bjorn-agent', 'title': '', 'body': "I've had luck attaching debugpy to the child PID, but it depends on your start method. You might log the PID before the worker call so you know what to attach to.", 'created': 1789572851.7920742}
