{'id': 88, 'parent_id': 87, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'ash-k', 'title': '', 'body': "Collection happens before fixtures resolve, so that error often means the value isn't available yet. I'd check the indirect docs and whether you actually need request fixture access there.", 'created': 1790108707.9692771}
{'id': 89, 'parent_id': 87, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'devon.r', 'title': '', 'body': "Without a minimal repro it's hard to say, but moving the setup inside the test body usually sidesteps the collection-time issue. Not always the cleanest, though.", 'created': 1790223723.4167886}
{'id': 90, 'parent_id': 87, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'pkrause', 'title': '', 'body': "I'd reduce it to one parametrized test and run with -q --collect-only. That often makes the collection order obvious.", 'created': 1790282137.020558}
{'id': 92, 'parent_id': 91, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'devon.r', 'title': '', 'body': 'Does it fail only in the full suite, or also when you run that one file? I’d start by checking fixture scope and any module-level state the fixture touches.', 'created': 1790490217.2061837}
{'id': 93, 'parent_id': 91, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'pkrause', 'title': '', 'body': 'Running pytest --setup-show usually makes fixture ordering obvious. Not a fix, but it narrows things down fast.', 'created': 1790489691.881873}
{'id': 95, 'parent_id': 94, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'mbot.ops', 'title': '', 'body': 'I’d time each hook individually first. Sometimes one slow hook is hiding in the list, and stages make it worse.', 'created': 1790828939.18357}
{'id': 96, 'parent_id': 94, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'juniper_ci', 'title': '', 'body': 'Check whether it’s recreating environments on every run. That’s often the difference between a few seconds and a coffee break.', 'created': 1790775724.4684198}
{'id': 98, 'parent_id': 97, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'devon.r', 'title': '', 'body': "If you've got a conftest inside tests/unit and another in tests/integration, each gets its own session cache. That bit me last month and I spent an hour blaming scope.", 'created': 1791180278.8926458}
{'id': 99, 'parent_id': 97, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'marta_codes', 'title': '', 'body': "Worth running with --setup-show, it prints when fixtures get torn down. Doesn't tell you why, but the duplicate becomes obvious fast.", 'created': 1791225718.9053}
{'id': 100, 'parent_id': 97, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'tkoh', 'title': '', 'body': "Also possible a module-scoped fixture is requesting it and pytest promotes things in a way you didn't expect. What does your fixture dependency graph look like?", 'created': 1791228061.437423}

